 "applies_to": "Heat-Timer SRC Platinum steam heating control for a burner/valve or district steam valve, with the BACnet IP/MS/TP board.",
 "summary": "The SRC Platinum controls steam heating on outdoor temperature, either through a burner/valve or a modulating district steam valve with position feedback or timed control. Its BACnet board exposes the settings, valve trims and position, schedule slots and sensor readings as Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values with instances in steps of 100.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Objects are Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values only. Rows without a read-only mark in the manual are listed as writable.",
  "Temperature objects use °F or °C depending on the INMODE (sensor type/mode) setting.",
  "Start-up settings can be read but not written over BACnet; Heat-Timer says to set them at the panel first.",
  "The manual prints some rows as ranges (SCHEDULES00-55 = 2700-2755). Only the first and last printed objects of each range are listed here; the ones in between follow the same pattern.",
  "CUTOFFPCT is printed with an asterisk in the manual; the footnote is not explained on the page.",
  "BOOSTADJ is printed with the range \"0 1 - 6 4\" (decimal points appear to be missing).",
  "Variable list: manual pages 18-19."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "The SRC runs steam heating (burner/valve or a district steam valve) on outdoor temperature. From the BMS, read the system and outdoor temperatures, the valve position and the burner status; adjust the system setpoint or heat adjustments, set a manual valve target, and force a day/night shift if needed.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
